From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:49:31 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] Preview tools: the floating preview draws the agent's
 cursor; resize answers with the new size; snapshots don't flash on screen

- The floating preview draws the agent's cursor over a Plutonium tab, on the
  layout the tab publishes for it, as the panel does.
- preview_resize on a desktop tab waits (up to 3 s) for the page to take a
  fixed size and answers with what the page reports, not the size before.
- Snapshots capture the viewport as drawn and shrink the PNG on the server.
  A scaled capture made Chromium emulate other device metrics for a moment,
  which a tab on screen showed as the page at 1/devicePixelRatio size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
